  "result": "I've written the revised record for NRS_484B_270_4 to `record.jsonl`; it hasn't been through the gate again yet. The only real fix is to the `blind` scenario: it now masks `kin.speed` instead of `rel.occupies`.\n\n**Why it failed:** with `rel.occupies` masked, the subsection 3 rule this node depends on (`NRS_484B_270_3_o2`) can't decide anything, because its look-backs and look-aheads all read whether x is in the lane. So `blind` always came out unknown for the wrong reason (\"window truncated\") rather than because of the masked data. The coder showed this across several different scenes, so no change to the scene could have fixed it.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`blind` scenario:** it masks `kin.speed`, which only this rule reads, through `drv.motion.moving` (the \"while driving\" part of s4). Occupancy stays observed, so the subsection 3 rule still decides as it does in `forbid`. Its exception (c) uses predicted closest approach, which works from velocity and position, not `kin.speed`. The narrative now says this.\n- **Small fixes:** the s3 narrowing now has `kind: \"reading\"`. I dropped the `p.motion_speed_tolerance` proposal because that parameter is already in the catalogue, and also dropped the `planned_on` field.\n- **Unchanged:** the mappings, the composition with subsection 3, the applicability and obligation, and the other four scenarios. `forbid`, `permit`, `idle` and `branch_1` already pass.\n\nThe coder's existing `blind` witness masks `rel.occupies`, so it needs one change to mask `kin.speed` instead. Nothing else in the Lean needs to change.",
